' ==============================================================================
' @file 4-5-crisismap-report-SM.puml
' @brief Conceptual state machine modeling system operating modes and infrastructure availability.
'
' @details
' This artifact utilizes orthogonal regions (concurrent states) to model the global 
' system behavior of Crisis Map. It captures two independent but parallel lifecycles: 
' the business-domain alert level (Crisis management mode) and the infrastructure 
' health status (Service availability).
'
' System Requirements Addressed:
' This diagram dictates the high-level operational requirements by defining:
' - The valid progression of crisis escalation and de-escalation protocols.
' - The fallback availability modes during partial external service outages.
' - The concurrent execution of business operations and infrastructure monitoring.
'
' Author(s): Vlado Sruk
' Context: Software Engineering Course / Project Documentation
'
' AI Usage Disclosure:
' Designed by Vlado Sruk. Generative AI tools were utilized for linguistic 
' revision, inline commenting, and structural formatting of the header. The author 
' has comprehensively reviewed, validated, and modified all AI-generated outputs, 
' assuming full responsibility for the final architectural logic.
'
' Traceability Note:
' The global states defined herein must be structurally verifiable in the implemented 
' system (e.g., via configuration flags, active incident aggregates, and health endpoints). 
' Any deviations between these modeled operational protocols and the final deployed 
' system behaviors must be retroactively updated to maintain evidence chain 
' completeness.
'
' Diagram level: System-Level Behavioral Design
' Diagram type:  State Machine Diagram
' ==============================================================================

@startuml
 
' ==============================================================================
' Global System Context with Extended State Variables
' ==============================================================================
state "Crisis Map operation" as Operation {
  
  ' Extended State Variables
  Operation : activeVerifiedDisasters : Integer = 0
  Operation : failedMapPings : Integer = 0

  ' ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  ' Orthogonal Region 1: Business Domain Operations
  ' ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  state "Crisis management mode" as Mode {
    [*] --> Routine
    state "Routine monitoring" as Routine
    state "Heightened watch" as Watch
    state "Active crisis" as Active
    state "Follow-up" as FollowUp

    Routine --> Watch : coordinator raises alert level
    Watch --> Routine : threat ruled out
    
    ' Utilizing state variable in Map Condition [...]
    Routine --> Active : disaster verified [activeVerifiedDisasters > 0] / publish advisory
    Watch --> Active : disaster verified [activeVerifiedDisasters > 0] / publish advisory
    
    ' Cannot end response until all active disasters are resolved
    Active --> FollowUp : response ended [activeVerifiedDisasters == 0]
    
    FollowUp --> Active : new verified disaster [activeVerifiedDisasters > 0]
    FollowUp --> Routine : follow-up completed
  }

  --

  ' ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  ' Orthogonal Region 2: Infrastructure Health Monitoring
  ' ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  state "Service availability" as Availability {
    [*] --> Online
    state "Online" as Online
    state "Limited: map unavailable" as Limited
    state "Unavailable: backend unreachable" as Unavailable

    ' Utilizing state variable for fault tolerance threshold
    Online --> Limited : map provider fails [failedMapPings >= 3]
    Limited --> Online : map provider recovers [failedMapPings == 0]
    
    Online --> Unavailable : backend becomes unreachable
    Limited --> Unavailable : backend becomes unreachable
    
    Unavailable --> Online : backend recovers [failedMapPings == 0]
    Unavailable --> Limited : backend recovers [failedMapPings >= 3]
  }
}
@enduml